# Units this dir used to deploy and must now be absent on every station.
# One basename per line (blank lines and #-comments ignored). The OTA
# install-systemd hook (apply_removals + _systemd_remover) disables+stops and
# removes each on deploy.
#
# Add an entry whenever you delete/rename a *.service that was previously
# shipped, so the removal propagates to already-provisioned stations.

# Renamed to ctt-board-detect.service (the tool now named for what it does:
# boot-time board detection + hardware identity).
ctt-station-id.service

# Removed: the V2 GPS-HAT kick. New boards have onboard GPS, so the HAT and its
# boot-time GPIO pulse are gone; this branch ships only on the new image.
ctt-gps-kick.service

# Removed: an unused oneshot placeholder (ExecStart=/bin/true) intended to group
# the ctt-* services so `systemctl stop ctt` would stop them all via PartOf —
# but nothing was ever wired to it, so it controlled nothing. Dropped until that
# grouping is actually implemented.
ctt.service

# Removed: the standalone LED gpio-led overlay service. It managed its own
# config.txt block independently of ctt-buttons-overlay; two append-at-end
# managers fought over block order and rebooted each other (V2 reboot loop). The
# LED migration is being redone as a single unified board device-tree config;
# until then V2 status LEDs use the in-process path. Purge the orphaned unit so
# it stops re-adding its block + looping on already-updated stations.
ctt-leds-overlay.service

# Replaced by ctt-device-config.service. These per-subsystem overlays each
# dynamically rewrote /boot/config.txt at boot (append a managed block / sed the
# RTC line) and rebooted on a diff — two append-at-end managers fought and
# rebooted each other (the V2 loop). ctt-device-config copies one complete static
# config.txt per revision instead. Purge the old units so nothing else edits
# config.txt on already-provisioned stations.
ctt-rtc-overlay.service
ctt-buttons-overlay.service

# NOTE: ctt-modem-provision.service was once retired here (the RNDIS auto-provisioner,
# 0ba6ce3) but is RE-INTRODUCED as the idempotent ECM boot GUARD (ADR 0003). It is
# therefore intentionally NOT in this removal list — the install loop deploys the new
# unit content, overwriting any stale copy. Do not re-add it here.
